{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 494 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "7da107c6ad53c12a7446c2ddfdf77603787526bcb2a16c418c539e6d99a84c09" :edb/db-before-t 493 :edb/db-after-t 494 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533806 50 #inst "2026-10-05T02:01:32.230Z" 13194139533806 true] [17592186115277 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252586 13194139533806 true] [17592186115277 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252590 13194139533806 true] [17592186115277 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252594 13194139533806 true] [17592186115277 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252597 13194139533806 true] [17592186115277 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252624 13194139533806 true] [17592186115278 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252600 13194139533806 true] [17592186115278 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252603 13194139533806 true] [17592186115278 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252606 13194139533806 true] [17592186115278 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252609 13194139533806 true] [17592186115279 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252558 13194139533806 true] [17592186115279 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252613 13194139533806 true] [17592186115279 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252617 13194139533806 true] [17592186115279 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252620 13194139533806 true] [17592186115280 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252565 13194139533806 true] [17592186115280 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252572 13194139533806 true] [17592186115280 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252579 13194139533806 true] [17592186115280 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252631 13194139533806 true] [17592186115280 1020 #edb/ref 17592186252638 13194139533806 true] [17592186115594 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533806 true] [17592186115594 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2},$ where $\\theta =m∠A.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ opposite to $∠A.$ Hence, we can use the sine ratio to find the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{8}{AB} \\\\ AB & =8(2) \\\\ AB & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the Pythagorean Theorem to find the missing side $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\sqrt{A{B}^{2}-B{C}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{16}^{2}-{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{256-64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{192} \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8\\cdot (8\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =32\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533806 true] [17592186115595 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533806 true] [17592186115595 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=5.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ 5 & =\\frac{2x+4}{x-1} \\\\ 5(x-1) & =2x+4 \\\\ 5x-5 & =2x+4 \\\\ 3x & =9 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =2x+4=2(3)+4=10, \\\\ AC & =x-1=3-1=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252558 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252559 13194139533806 true] [17592186252558 1089 "q-124466" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252558 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533806 true] [17592186252558 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/4784e18b0e3631272efa1c002e686e9349ea04a900d8bc1e6b0416c09e994ccb.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{5}{3},$ calculate the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." 13194139533806 true] [17592186252558 1113 #uuid "ee965f67-bb44-5997-ae93-829735f50901" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252558 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{5}{3},$ where $\\theta =m∠B.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{AB}$ adjacent to $∠B.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to find the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{AC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{5}{3} & =\\frac{AC}{18} \\\\ \\frac{5}{3}\\cdot 18 & =AC \\\\ AC & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot AB \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 30\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =270.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252560 13194139533806 true] [17592186252559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252561 13194139533806 true] [17592186252559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252562 13194139533806 true] [17592186252559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252563 13194139533806 true] [17592186252559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252564 13194139533806 true] [17592186252559 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533806 true] [17592186252559 1041 "selection" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252559 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252560 13194139533806 true] [17592186252559 1110 #uuid "0e9da70e-743e-522d-b545-2ea535a8382b" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252560 1034 "270" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252560 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252560 1111 #uuid "d7a25d3d-74ea-56ed-8931-14f46984d29a" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252561 1034 "180" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252561 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252561 1111 #uuid "12e72070-ddac-5240-a4f3-e64f07645843" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252562 1034 "210" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252562 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252562 1111 #uuid "e3c3a4f1-4bd3-5fdb-9510-756ad4769b5d" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252563 1034 "150" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252563 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252563 1111 #uuid "01c1ef96-e707-5873-9dc2-04854dcb41ab" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252564 1034 "240" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252564 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252564 1111 #uuid "f0b35384-c99a-56ac-b1f5-ea1ceabfec87" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252565 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252566 13194139533806 true] [17592186252565 1089 "q-124470" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252565 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533806 true] [17592186252565 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/5c7116b4ee933aacb284e0d9b16576b910166bf1e01f58a46931fc0636a933c5.png)\n\nFind the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." 13194139533806 true] [17592186252565 1113 #uuid "c661f073-d3a4-584b-af91-436e2a5fe0cc" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252565 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={30}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}\\,x}{5x+2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}\\,x}{5x+2} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(5x+2) & =3\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ 5\\sqrt{3}\\,x+2\\sqrt{3} & =6\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{3} & =\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =2\\sqrt{3}\\,x=2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 2=4\\sqrt{3}, \\\\ AB & =5x+2=5(2)+2=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot BC\\cdot AB \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =24\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252567 13194139533806 true] [17592186252566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252568 13194139533806 true] [17592186252566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252569 13194139533806 true] [17592186252566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252570 13194139533806 true] [17592186252566 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252571 13194139533806 true] [17592186252566 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533806 true] [17592186252566 1041 "selection" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252566 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252568 13194139533806 true] [17592186252566 1110 #uuid "f0745145-08f0-5e22-ba56-c5b6e3447a31" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252567 1034 "20\\sqrt{3}" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252567 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252567 1111 #uuid "63eedc9b-db3e-581b-9940-2913e71e796e" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252568 1034 "24\\sqrt{3}" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252568 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252568 1111 #uuid "7cf34dda-628b-57bd-b350-78befeae4976" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252569 1034 "40" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252569 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252569 1111 #uuid "c3b6bea3-e9d9-50e5-a9b6-27e8f753a19f" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252570 1034 "36" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252570 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252570 1111 #uuid "3e01d1a2-1c50-52e1-a59b-0070bde853a3" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252571 1034 "16\\sqrt{3}" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252571 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252571 1111 #uuid "dc38716b-0b31-5603-a6cc-89db61be99fe" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252572 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252573 13194139533806 true] [17592186252572 1089 "q-124471" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252572 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533806 true] [17592186252572 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/f0d4e8ddf3a1b6cacab75f3207575695de5790f8223e30bc948e93daf37c939f.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to one decimal place, find the area of $△ABC$ shown above." 13194139533806 true] [17592186252572 1113 #uuid "3fa83370-246b-52a5-bb67-0622bfb629ec" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252572 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={30}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =\\frac{x-1}{x+2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})(x+2) & =x-1 \\\\ x\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})+2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =x-1 \\\\ x\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})-x & =-1-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\ x(\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})-1) & =-1-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\ x(1-\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})) & =1+2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1+2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})}{1-\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})} \\\\ x & =5.098\\,0…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =x-1=5.098\\,0-1=4.098\\,0…, \\\\ AB & =x+2=5.098\\,0+2=7.098\\,0….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}(4.098\\,0…)(7.098\\,0…) \\\\  & =14.543\\,8… \\\\  & ≈14.5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the one decimal place." 13194139533806 true] [17592186252573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252574 13194139533806 true] [17592186252573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252575 13194139533806 true] [17592186252573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252576 13194139533806 true] [17592186252573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252577 13194139533806 true] [17592186252573 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252578 13194139533806 true] [17592186252573 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533806 true] [17592186252573 1041 "selection" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252573 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252574 13194139533806 true] [17592186252573 1110 #uuid "2bfeb9d4-a048-5bc6-a337-af552ccd8e41" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252574 1034 "14.5" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252574 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252574 1111 #uuid "fddca52e-d8ec-5acd-9f04-b74ff4127577" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252575 1034 "12.4" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252575 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252575 1111 #uuid "27248f76-3fcd-503e-8827-718b9ab3bd92" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252576 1034 "16.3" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252576 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252576 1111 #uuid "2a66f2ae-5e03-57b7-a978-dbdc33db814e" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252577 1034 "13.4" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252577 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252577 1111 #uuid "969e0922-6fdc-522d-8dcd-0e7cbf944a51" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252578 1034 "15.6" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252578 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252578 1111 #uuid "bfc3f6a0-4ad8-531b-a05a-d49e1e9d895e" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252579 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252580 13194139533806 true] [17592186252579 1089 "q-124475" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252579 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533806 true] [17592186252579 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/0ad5279a7ec9ac20a2c4e1449f93ae67854caf021aba8435165b80069f23afbd.png)\n\nFind the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." 13194139533806 true] [17592186252579 1113 #uuid "963a40ef-ec42-5f96-ad58-c048d492c81f" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252579 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠B={60}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠B,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{AC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({60}^{∘}) & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}\\,x}{x+2} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}\\,x}{x+2} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(x+2) & =2\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\,x+2\\sqrt{3} & =2\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{3} & =\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =2\\sqrt{3}\\,x=2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 2=4\\sqrt{3}, \\\\ AB & =x+2=2+2=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AC\\cdot AB \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252581 13194139533806 true] [17592186252580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252582 13194139533806 true] [17592186252580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252583 13194139533806 true] [17592186252580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252584 13194139533806 true] [17592186252580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252585 13194139533806 true] [17592186252580 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533806 true] [17592186252580 1041 "selection" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252580 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252583 13194139533806 true] [17592186252580 1110 #uuid "4c495a22-3a33-5b67-929e-2652b984c5bc" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252581 1034 "\\frac{9\\sqrt{3}}{2}" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252581 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252581 1111 #uuid "703fe4a2-8381-563d-a086-8d740b5e8f9a" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252582 1034 "6\\sqrt{3}" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252582 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252582 1111 #uuid "73fcb0dc-f733-515b-9bdd-bd69d99c2aff" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252583 1034 "8\\sqrt{3}" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252583 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252583 1111 #uuid "1a730108-7698-514a-a07e-3658f58d2c20" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252584 1034 "4\\sqrt{3}" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252584 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252584 1111 #uuid "72905faa-6ec6-5e72-aad8-deab943eb