10 #uuid "5002344a-229b-5afb-8703-6daff5817d3a" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252602 1034 "5" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252602 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252602 1111 #uuid "1c4f597d-80b6-54bb-b310-968ef151ea20" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252603 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252604 13194139533806 true] [17592186252603 1089 "q-251086" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252603 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533806 true] [17592186252603 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/51e60c645aa6be034a8ef23d16a9ca7a815ca15fe815d7c3b03a866e693f3e5b.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=\\frac{2}{3},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139533806 true] [17592186252603 1113 #uuid "89d89b73-504a-5f33-91c3-a6a449c6798e" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252603 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=\\frac{2}{3}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & =\\frac{10x-1}{8x+2} \\\\ 2(8x+2) & =3(10x-1) \\\\ 16x+4 & =30x-3 \\\\ 14x & =7 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =10x-1=10(\\frac{1}{2})-1=4, \\\\ AC & =8x+2=8(\\frac{1}{2})+2=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252604 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252605 13194139533806 true] [17592186252604 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533806 true] [17592186252604 1041 "field-1" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252604 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252605 13194139533806 true] [17592186252604 1110 #uuid "2b1d34d4-3efb-5490-a42e-fc7d33a1f42e" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252605 1034 "12" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252605 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252605 1111 #uuid "1297785f-656c-5acc-9e1b-5dc1c3f4ba2a" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252606 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252607 13194139533806 true] [17592186252606 1089 "q-251087" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252606 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533806 true] [17592186252606 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/05003be9090f98f39a65d9ec33e8568fa43ec5c427e34398e4932708f8a03ccc.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=4,$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139533806 true] [17592186252606 1113 #uuid "213eedb1-565d-5f76-b007-4e78dbc869a4" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252606 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=4.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ 4 & =\\frac{11x-12}{x+4} \\\\ 4(x+4) & =11x-12 \\\\ 4x+16 & =11x-12 \\\\ 7x & =28 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =11x-12=11(4)-12=32, \\\\ AC & =x+4=4+4=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 32\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =128.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252607 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252608 13194139533806 true] [17592186252607 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533806 true] [17592186252607 1041 "field-1" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252607 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252608 13194139533806 true] [17592186252607 1110 #uuid "130001a8-a8c5-56f9-81ea-43f1bd107e68" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252608 1034 "128" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252608 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252608 1111 #uuid "86491e84-7a31-5e30-990e-33a0e59a7d7a" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252609 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252610 13194139533806 true] [17592186252609 1089 "q-251089" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252609 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533806 true] [17592186252609 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/251ca3005dd302ec1e7ba0c7d7c497e28fd4c16cc0e431cc3691bdd4fe65446a.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\frac{1}{5},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139533806 true] [17592186252609 1113 #uuid "c972b721-661a-53b1-be3e-5e738f66bd5d" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252609 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\frac{1}{5}.$ Notice that relative to $∠B,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\frac{1}{5} & =\\frac{6x-1}{15x} \\\\ 15x & =5(6x-1) \\\\ 15x & =30x-5 \\\\ 15x & =5 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =15x=15(\\frac{1}{3})=5, \\\\ AC & =6x-1=6(\\frac{1}{3})-1=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252610 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252611 13194139533806 true] [17592186252610 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252612 13194139533806 true] [17592186252610 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533806 true] [17592186252610 1041 "field-1" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252610 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252611 13194139533806 true] [17592186252610 1110 #uuid "ed72c7f2-e36a-56d1-b136-fae8c66f4f9c" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252611 1034 "\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252611 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252611 1111 #uuid "600b45b3-9266-5373-85b7-d2067f0f81ae" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252612 1034 "5" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252612 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252612 1111 #uuid "4e44e423-5df9-50ca-b8ea-ec0d624532cf" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252613 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252614 13194139533806 true] [17592186252613 1089 "q-251121" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252613 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533806 true] [17592186252613 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/214774fb428c62ad5131760c2a073690bca63f6b8bb06131c4381fee943597c3.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =2,$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139533806 true] [17592186252613 1113 #uuid "6e4f2531-54a0-5be4-a41b-03ab9dce1975" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252613 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =2,$ where $\\theta =m∠A.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ adjacent to $∠A.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to find the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{BC}{15} \\\\ BC & =2\\cdot 15 \\\\ BC & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 30\\cdot 15 \\\\  & =225.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252614 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252615 13194139533806 true] [17592186252614 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252616 13194139533806 true] [17592186252614 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533806 true] [17592186252614 1041 "field-1" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252614 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252616 13194139533806 true] [17592186252614 1110 #uuid "3e504436-4023-5f4b-99f4-15f12e0a9269" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252615 1034 "450" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252615 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252615 1111 #uuid "0c086cd4-1d45-5818-901a-8e06b11d2b37" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252616 1034 "225" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252616 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252616 1111 #uuid "3a5fa6d7-3d77-55f1-aa75-b9f548fa982c" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252617 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252618 13194139533806 true] [17592186252617 1089 "q-251126" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252617 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533806 true] [17592186252617 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/ef2b0447e81370a50ea6d4115fc6f4687aff74fee17bc66f116b3c732667857e.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{2}{7},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139533806 true] [17592186252617 1113 #uuid "3a1be4ef-1b5d-5162-b0ca-0628ac21678e" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252617 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{2}{7},$ where $\\theta =m∠B.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ adjacent to $∠B.$ Hence, we can use the cosine ratio to find the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{2}{7} & =\\frac{4}{AB} \\\\ AB & =\\frac{4}{2}\\cdot 7 \\\\ AB & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the Pythagorean Theorem to find the missing side $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\sqrt{A{B}^{2}-B{C}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{14}^{2}-{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{196-16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{180} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\sqrt{5}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =12\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252618 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252619 13194139533806 true] [17592186252618 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533806 true] [17592186252618 1041 "field-1" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252618 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252619 13194139533806 true] [17592186252618 1110 #uuid "72938f94-b6fb-512e-adeb-21228d24c46d" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252619 1034 "12\\sqrt{5}" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252619 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252619 1111 #uuid "c98fc282-138a-506a-8540-d4695139aef2" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252620 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252621 13194139533806 true] [17592186252620 1089 "q-251130" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252620 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533806 true] [17592186252620 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/6b1c6c90b25fa7c4cd4cde42bdcd5e69a2ccef63f1945067a8f62dc7ee779f05.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{7},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." 13194139533806 true] [17592186252620 1113 #uuid "e75dd5d8-326f-57e3-93b1-3e0bc2ea6f68" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252620 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{7},$ where $\\theta =m∠A.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ opposite to $∠A.$ Hence, we can use the sine ratio to find the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{7} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{AB} \\\\ AB & =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{\\sqrt{13}}\\cdot 7 \\\\ AB & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the Pythagorean Theorem to find the missing side $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\sqrt{A{B}^{2}-B{C}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{7}^{2}-(\\sqrt{13})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49-13} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{13}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252621 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252622 13194139533806 true] [17592186252621 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252623 13194139533806 true] [17592186252621 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533806 true] [17592186252621 1041 "field-1" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252621 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252623 13194139533806 true] [17592186252621 1110 #uuid "f41d44f4-bb54-5588-9a0b-9481c1ca932b" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252622 1034 "6\\sqrt{13}" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252622 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252622 1111 #uuid "cb248702-f541-551e-a9bf-d40ac94171d0" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252623 1034 "3\\sqrt{13}" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252623 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252623 1111 #uuid "0c34f093-88d1-5c79-bea4-5cc38aeabc99" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252624 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252625 13194139533806 true] [17592186252624 1089 "q-28308" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252624 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533806 true] [17592186252624 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/43e5ba6bff8a20c20f8be2b18d57ad07fc030477d589a2ba43da0f2cb3816587.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the nearest integer, what is the area of $△ABC$ shown above?" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252624 1113 #uuid "f806f6d9-b146-5a87-9874-1eb64a7a1553" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252624 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nNotice that relative to the given angle $∠B,$ we have the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and need to determine the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({40}^{∘}) & =\\frac{20}{BC} \\\\ BC\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({40}^{∘}) & =20 \\\\ BC & =\\frac{20}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡({40}^{∘})} \\\\ BC & =23.835…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 20\\cdot (23.835…) \\\\  & =238.350… \\\\  & ≈238,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." 13194139533806 true] [17592186252625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252626 13194139533806 true] [17592186252625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252627 13194139533806 true] [17592186252625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252628 13194139533806 true] [17592186252625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252629 13194139533806 true] [17592186252625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252630 13194139533806 true] [17592186252625 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533806 true] [17592186252625 1041 "selection" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252625 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252627 13194139533806 true] [17592186252625 1110 #uuid "46230c9e-658d-5100-bb7f-79917ee1b44e" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252626 1034 "241" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252626 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252626 1111 #uuid "22b1cb37-20ee-52fb-8882-b8b4c2f5c200" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252627 1034 "238" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252627 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252627 1111 #uuid "17984ca8-7d3a-5510-8343-726a4e82c6c5" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252628 1034 "236" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252628 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252628 1111 #uuid "9a9cf4f4-033d-5e68-ae76-6a09fdcadad0" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252629 1034 "245" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252629 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252629 1111 #uuid "dc189ced-daed-5439-a00d-0cfca665c5bc" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252630 1034 "233" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252630 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533806 true] [17592186252630 1111 #uuid "8d9f080a-f9d3-56ac-a070-100df577f177" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252631 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252632 13194139533806 true] [17592186252631 1089 "q-76773" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252631 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533806 true] [17592186252631 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/ca9c6640b6cb239ae19b195731d8f605adae8826f66e10b075f7b0ad4a60690f.png)\n\nFind the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." 13194139533806 true] [17592186252631 1113 #uuid "da752c15-1fa7-5b59-b50f-3601de203814" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252631 1145 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={30}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,x}{x+4} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,x}{x+4} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(x+4) & =3\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\,x+4\\sqrt{3} & =3\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ -2\\sqrt{3}\\,x & =-4\\sqrt{3} \\\\ x & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{2\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =\\sqrt{3}\\,x=\\sqrt{3}(2)=2\\sqrt{3}, \\\\ AB & =x+4=2+4=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533806 true] [17592186252632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252633 13194139533806 true] [17592186252632 1000 #edb/ref 1759218